  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_bc6624d35ce042c184f95e5da1067cbf",
      "statement": "`celld_logic::on_event` is the single way behavioral state advances; both the production executor and the deterministic simulator feed it events and perform the returned effects, and no adapter may mutate `State` directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L5-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf8b37a9ee1fc07e9a574b6df6d477168c0bbc44e5b215ec8e9fdf483a7c6986:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L3-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d17ba561785ca7348bb778cc922706279fc2c8177e57be65f95ad2d2ff6c06b8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L5215-L5215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92f95be291fcb6f971dcbe55a0f08e0ff402a7f05be7f4f04c6c5abc504c7f57:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d66755818eef4b1899b59d6c51a6b74f",
      "statement": "Node authority is the lease's published validity evaluated at ask time on the monotonic clock (`State::node_authoritative`), so a holder whose lease lapsed must answer false even before the fence timer fires; a suspended VM's timer fires late but a request evaluated after resume still refuses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L714-L737",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6085ed359ef13e7c64247f04dc411bad80b8d85a8dee6fe0eaa9b9e982fbee5b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e19efbe4ed1a401d8fa5f9e9ba40af35",
      "statement": "The core never reads a clock or a proc file itself; events carry sampled wall-clock and monotonic timestamps, and `on_event` updates the remembered clock instants from them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L5183-L5213",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0fd15ecd3b3d43a879459c0b97d813a9b3972b4cfb3922c80b9ce4b0c4b666f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1499a130231b444bbfa39f973a6e88bc",
      "statement": "Each cell moves through an explicit `Phase` enum mapping onto the Durable Objects lifecycle states, with `Resident` (in memory), `Dormant` (out of memory but still owned, hibernated when sockets survive), and `Inactive` (owned by nobody, initial state) as the top-level states amid many transient phases.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L92-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92ff51365b437c3c534993fa7b99630f64ab8bcd2e0ba5b429fcc76fed11c500:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86476abe94114bcea46668e69241848b",
      "statement": "Operator-visible phase names come from `phase_name` and `phase_census` reports counts per phase; the names are stable across internal renames because charts and humans read them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L214-L240",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2784119a349944f22e98d6f9d9876e374a3e653c9d6c37709aefbc48538dff83:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L977-L983",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39d41371f333eb64d703340948026942c161c5b7fde9d9a783ed54040f3c4998:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d911e10eca3b4155aca6de099edfb2ae",
      "statement": "Residency is a hard cap counted exactly (`max_resident`), and admission additionally refuses when the node is shedding; `has_capacity` refuses more work but holds what it has rather than shedding a live cell it must place elsewhere.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1369-L1377",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:324a5af1f21248e75835f8599c364b284934ac55302a65d2043544c8e2605b68:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L63-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:321be400a63b0da4c82732116e090dde3f77d5ccfdd1125bf2ce61fefd66865f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27ceb6e822ad4d159616f5d01ade4756",
      "statement": "Cells waiting for a residency slot park in a FIFO `capacity_waiters` queue; FIFO is the whole admission policy because waking every waiter and letting them race is unfair under sustained eviction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L546-L550",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e424a5e6ca0b5ee4c9f9bd0a9c126a7d937de3b0c3f45296e9150c7e5533bea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_44c8d260670c42238bb8d8bb0b576602",
      "statement": "The output gate applies one durability rule to every output `Channel` via `State::output`: a write opens its own barrier and waits for a proof covering its position, a read-only output trails the newest barrier on its cell, and the core never branches on which channel it is.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L3-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee7e341223b08fbc669192b8f73617f33a8f96091da975a6c49fb67c9e29090d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L67-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c922c5b92035a2b5c70fb428859b5e893c13875e6c019d4fda739eb7fbdf79ce:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L334-L369",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2b2308f503f385d5d0c535b72738baf285a1b201a66e281388b137523fbd7bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2cc3931c830a4e0eb2527537026f45cb",
      "statement": "A bucket-proof gate additionally requires `VerifyOwnership` (reading the record still names this node at this epoch) before anything is revealed, because durable in `e<epoch>/` is not durable if the prefix was orphaned; a fleet proof needs no read because the ensemble arbitrated it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L173-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fc9ab050354091b407d2391b1a217f89ea1cbfa33c9beb523726911f448e551:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e8f5a898c0041e9a59195cfed410c2d",
      "statement": "A gate drained by a fence or deadline fails the write rather than acknowledging it into an orphaned lineage, and the cell is reset (`reset_cell`) on an unproven write.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L232-L285",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9acd29a789362b732c5d59e948528a91ff22e4855752a801fc9540e247c59dca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8c38f18e34e4787aa160464889ead68",
      "statement": "Memory-pressure shedding is a pure classifier of a memory sample plus the prior shedding latch, driven by `Event::LoadSampled`; residency is not part of it because residency is capped at admission.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L49-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70ddd2dae0657066e691ed68a5c779a81dbe99f5933f0c367f048929a12984f2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L7-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7e36a3b700fa1110b1332e3a0f99500369f37d45edbd98a09b3e5288f0fe94e8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_662e51b19c59489b9bcfb5cce07f4146",
      "statement": "Shedding holds the node until every configured low watermark clears (the `Latches` hysteresis), so it walks down to its target instead of oscillating around its ceiling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L4673-L4679",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3557428dcc2690030787a74bf96a81d46a757d83ed4c51827fb41e47fb70e702:"
